From 4f34e278052c6798d5edbf5209af81c4afb5efd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sleep-walker <sleep_walker@gnu.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:28:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bump gorilla/websocket to v1.5.3 and x/crypto to v0.56.0
 (security)

gorilla/websocket@1.5.0 used math/rand (predictable) instead of
crypto/rand for WebSocket frame mask key generation (GO-2026-6278,
CVSS 6.9) -- reachable via the remoteauth/QR-login websocket flow per
govulncheck call-graph analysis, unlike the telegram/whatsapp x/crypto
findings which were unreachable. This is the first bridge in the
migration series with an actually exploitable finding.

Also bumps golang.org/x/crypto to 0.56.0 (GO-2026-6354, GO-2026-6355,
same unreachable SSH-client DoS findings as the other bridges).
---
 go.mod | 6 +++---
 go.sum | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index 68d1bc0..2699c85 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
